      "problem": "Which of the following is undefined?\n\nI. $0\\cdot 0$\n\nII. $\\frac{2}{0}$\n\nIII. $\\frac{0}{-1}$",
      "worked_solution": "We consider each point individually:\n\n- Multiplying any number by zero always gives zero. Therefore, $0\\cdot 0=0.$\n\n- We cannot divide any number by zero. Therefore, $\\frac{2}{0}=2÷0$ is undefined.\n\n- Zero divided by any number (other than zero) equals zero. Therefore, $\\frac{0}{-1}=0÷(-1)=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
